From ee38ea9522f91da32f092457e8d082091866504a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:18:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core-update): checkpoint capped turns without
 retry-window loops [daveey] (#205)

* fix(core-update): checkpoint capped turns without retry-window loops [daveey]

* fix(core-update): parked capped pause keeps continuation eligibility [daveey]

A capped turn parked between drain windows was aged from started_at by the
in-place continue, the startup sweep and the notice hold, so under the default
15-min freshness a park longer than the window dropped the marker. Its live
writer now restamps parked_at while parking (and once as parking ends); all
three readers measure core_update_pause freshness via turn_marker.freshness_since.
